2. The articles and the questions: CC BY-NC-ND 4.0

   The place articles (content/articles/), the questions and their answers
   (content/questions/), in every language they are written or translated in, and the
   files the build makes of them (apps/web/public/data/articles/, the article text on the
   place pages, the question pages, api/v1/questions.json) are licensed under the
   Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0 International licence:
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/

   In short (the licence's own text governs): you may copy and share them unchanged,
   in any medium or format, on another site or in a collection too, with credit and
   the licence named, and not for commercial purposes. You may not share a changed or
   translated version of them. Credit: "History Globe (Vadym Arnaut), CC BY-NC-ND
   4.0", with a link to the page and to the licence. Short quotations with credit, as
   the law allows them, and links need no licence.

   Until 2026-10-17 these texts were offered under CC BY 4.0. Copies made under that
   licence keep it (a Creative Commons licence cannot be revoked); what is published
   from that date on is under this one.

   Text and data mining. For these texts, the copyright holder reserves the right to
   reproduce and extract them for text and data mining, within the meaning of Article
   4(3) of Directive (EU) 2019/790, including for the training, fine-tuning or
   evaluation of machine-learning models, as far as the licence above does not already
   permit the use. The site states the reservation in its robots.txt (the Disallow lines
   for training crawlers and the Content-Signal line, "ai-train=no") and in the
   "tdm-reservation: 1" header. Both are sent for the whole site, but the reservation
   covers this part only: every other part is under its own licence (the data CC BY
   4.0, the code AGPL-3.0-or-later, the script MIT, the examples CC0), which governs
   and which the reservation does not narrow.

3. The data: CC BY 4.0

   - The curated content in content/ other than articles/, questions/, docs/, reviews/,
     drafts/ and README.md: place names in every language, tours, events, battles, when towns stood,
     ancient-author notes, photo records and the rest;
   - the data the build makes from it: apps/web/public/data/ except articles/, photos/
     and verses/, the open API in apps/web/public/api/ except questions.json, and the
     route maps of the tours, apps/web/public/og/tour/*.jpg (the routes on Natural
     Earth, which is in the public domain);
   - the data files kept beside the code: pipeline/rivers/rivers.geojson (derived from
     RiverATLAS, CC BY 4.0), pipeline/rivers/targets.json,
     pipeline/ancient/names-cyrillic.json, pipeline/dataset_card.md, and the crosswalk
     tables docs/crosswalk/*.csv

   are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence:
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

   Credit: "History Globe (Vadym Arnaut), CC BY 4.0", with a link to the source where
   the medium allows.

   The theographic_* columns of docs/crosswalk/places.csv and docs/crosswalk/people.csv
   hold the record ids and lookup names of Theographic Bible Metadata (CC BY-SA 4.0),
   and in places.csv also the records Theographic itself takes for the same place
   (theographic_canonical, theographic_same_place_records). They are Theographic's, not
   licensed here: as far as they are protected, its CC BY-SA 4.0 applies to them. content/drafts/ holds Wikidata labels (CC0) and stays
   under CC0.

   Not licensed here: apps/web/public/data/photos/ holds Wikimedia Commons photographs,
   each under the licence its record names (content/photos.yaml; the place card and the
   place page show it), and apps/web/public/data/verses/ holds the Bible text of
   public-domain editions (docs/ATTRIBUTIONS.md, "Scripture").

4. The reviews

   The reviews in content/reviews/ belong to their authors. Each file names its author
   and the licence the author gave it (the "licence" field).

5. Third-party data, images and software

   Third-party data, images and software included or referenced here remain under their
   own licences (OpenBible.info, STEPBible TIPNR, Cliopatria, Pleiades, Itiner-e,
   RiverATLAS, Natural Earth, Copernicus WorldDEM-30 and the other elevation models,
   Wikimedia Commons photographs, the public-domain Bible editions, MapLibre, React,
   Lucide, the fonts and others); see docs/ATTRIBUTIONS.md and apps/web/public/licenses/.
   CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md is the Contributor Covenant, version 2.1
   (https://www.contributor-covenant.org), under CC BY 4.0, with the project's contact
   address added. The grants in parts 1 to 3 and the reservation in part 6 cover this
   project's own contribution only; they relicense and reserve none of these.

6. The name and the logo: not licensed

   The name "History Globe" and its logo (apps/web/public/favicon.*, icon-*.png,
   apple-touch-icon.png) are not licensed under any of the above. All rights reserved.

   The preview images (apps/web/public/og.jpg, og/<language>.jpg, shots/) are pictures
   of the site. The project's own part of them, its interface with the name and the
   logo, is not licensed either. What they show of the data and the texts keeps the
   licence of its part above, and what they show from third parties keeps its own
   licence (part 5): the borders from Cliopatria (CC BY 4.0), the relief from
   Copernicus WorldDEM-30 and the other elevation models, Natural Earth, and the
   photographs in the cards, each under the licence printed on it. In
   shots/*-place.jpg that is "Jerusalem Old City from the Mount of Olives" by Kok Leng
   Yeo, CC BY 2.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/); in shots/*-tour.jpg,
   "Herodes Atticus Bath near Alexandria Troas" by Raicem, CC BY 4.0
   (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
